  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Subject to appropriate safeguarding conditions, the proposed redevelopment of the site for housing would be compatible with the character of the residential area and the proposal would not harm the appearance of the street scene or neighbours' living conditions. The development would provide acceptable living conditions, and would accord with the Council's traffic and parking standards. The proposal complies with policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), H.1.1 (Location of New Housing Development), H.4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H.4.2 (Residential Density) and T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities For Developments).",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the buildings are occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development Order) 1995 (or any order revoking or re-enacting that order) no enlargement of the premises or any additional structures/buildings within the curtilage of the site shall be carried out.",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 08.00 to 18.00 on Mondays to Friday,08.00 to 13.00 on Saturdays and none on Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 (or any order revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification), no garages shall be erected [other than those expressly authorised by this permission].",
    "Condition : 7 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 8 - Landscaping and lighting details to be submitted - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscaping and lighting have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Such details shall include, boundary treatment, parking layouts, vehicle access, separate pedestrian access and planting plans, and the scheme shall not be implemented otherwise than in accordance with any approval given.  The details so approved shall be implemented before first occupation of the properties or (in the case of planting ) in the first available planting season after completion of the development.",
    "Condition : 9 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before the buildings are occupied or in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 10 - The garage or car parking accommodation shown on drawing No. 1282 PL 101C, received 07/10/05 shall be provided before the dwelling to which it relates is occupied and thereafter it shall not be used for any purpose other than the parking of vehicles.",
    "Condition : 11 - No development shall take place until details of proposed pedestrian access to and within the site have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.  These details shall be carried out as approved."
  ],
